course: dictionary
lesson: 9696
title: Suggest: an idea or a clue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suggest has two meanings. First, it means to give an idea or a plan for others to think about. In class, you might suggest ideas in a group, or drop a note in the suggestion box.
explain: Second, it means to show that something may be true, without saying it clearly. «Studies suggest that people who often give thanks tend to feel happier.» The studies do not say this for certain. They point towards it.
explain: Check the context to find which meaning fits. In «anyone can suggest "no phones at dinner"», it means offer an idea. In «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted», it means the research points towards this, but does not prove it.
fact: Suggest is a verb: suggest, suggests, suggested, suggesting.
fact: «Suggest» means to give an idea or plan for others to think about.
fact: «Suggest» can also mean to show that something may be true, without saying it clearly.
fact: Look out for the phrases «suggest that», «suggest doing» and «a suggestion box».
fact: «Suggestion» is the noun for the idea you offer.
exercise: «Anyone can suggest "no phones at dinner", as long as it's for everyone.» What does suggest mean here? | *Give an idea for others to think about | Shout loudly | Show that something is true without saying so | Forget
exercise: «Studies suggest that people who often give thanks tend to feel happier.» What does suggest mean here? | Order someone to do something | *Show that something may be true, without saying it clearly | Hide something | Tell a clear and certain fact
exercise: Ben put a note in the class suggestion box. Which word is the noun from the same family as suggest? | *Suggestion | Sure | Sugar | Question
test: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» What does suggests mean here? | *Points towards it, without saying it clearly | Forgets the daylight | Stops the risk | Proves for certain
test: Which sentence uses suggest to give an idea for others to think about? | «The sun is hot in summer.» | *«Harvey could suggest we all put our phones away at dinner.» | «The dog barked at the postman.» | «The bus was late again.»
exam: The scientist Robin Dunbar «suggested» a person can keep about 150 close relationships, and the number is still argued about. What does suggested mean here? | *Put forward an idea for others to think about | Proved for certain | Counted every person in a band | Forgot about it
